    coverageNote: "Read from Lehninger 8, the sterol thread that runs across two sections, on A printed pages 352-353 (the subheading Sterols Have Four Fused Carbon Rings, plus FIGURE 10-15 and the taurocholic acid structure, and the sterol bullets of SUMMARY 10.2), A printed page 356 (the subheading Steroid Hormones Carry Messages between Tissues, with FIGURE 10-18 in full and the isoprene structure printed on the same page), A printed page 357 (vitamin D as evidence that a sterol is a hormone precursor, taken only as far as this node needs it), and A printed page 360 (the closing sentence that gathers sterols, steroids, dolichols, vitamins A, E, D and K, ubiquinone and plastoquinone as one isoprene-derived family, and defers the pathway to chapter 21). FOR THE lehNote ONLY, two pages of Lehninger chapter 21 were also read directly in A and are cited as such: A printed page 774 (Stage 2, Condensation of Six Activated Isoprene Units to Form Squalene) and A printed page 792 (the printed pathway in the chapter's Data Analysis Problem, which prints the whole isoprene condensation series with every carbon count). COVERAGE IS DELIBERATELY MARKED partial, not full, and the reason should not be glossed: this node does not cover any complete Lehninger section. It follows one thread — the sterol and its descendants — across parts of 10.2 and 10.3, because that thread is what the Czech nodes carrying topicKey cholesterol-and-isoprenoids actually teach, while the rest of 10.2 belongs to L-10-2-1 and the rest of 10.3 to L-10-3-1. Section 21.4, the primary Lehninger mapping of this topicKey in topickey_assignment.json, is NOT covered here: two of its pages were read for one specific arbitration and nothing more. If §21.4 is ever written up properly it takes its own node and this one stays as the chapter-10 structural layer beneath it. WHAT THE CZECH NODES ALREADY HAVE: 8-4-3 is a short single-paragraph node holding one strong claim — that terpenoids and steroids are, as a rule, NOT metabolised by the organism that makes them for energy or carbon but excreted, their further fate not well mapped, and that cholesterol leaves the animal body only after prior conversion to bile acids and their salts; 9-27 covers secondary plant metabolites. Neighbouring Czech nodes under a different key hold the structures: 8-2-4-3 has squalene and the steran skeleton, 8-2-4-4 has the sterol definition (a C8 to C10 side chain at C-17 plus a hydroxyl at C-3), cholesterol at 0 to 40 per cent of membrane lipid and its contribution to rigidity, and the plant sterols. THIS NODE DOES NOT RESTATE THOSE. What it adds is the amphipathy argument (which group is the head and how long the body is), the exact sterol-versus-steroid distinction, the fact that bacteria cannot synthesise sterols, the sterol ester as the storage and transport form, bile acids read as DETERGENTS with the mechanism spelled out, the nanomolar potency of steroid hormones and their nuclear receptors, prednisone's mechanism through phospholipase A2, brassinolide, and the single sentence that unifies the whole isoprenoid family. ONE ARBITRATION IS CARRIED AS A lehNote and it points at Czech 8-3-8, following the arrangement leh_ch6b.js records: section 9f puts a lehNote on the Czech node, but this session was instructed to create one file and edit none, so the note lives here and points back. It should be moved onto 8-3-8 with its node field repointed the first time ch8.js is opened for editing.",
